   "id": "korea-samsung-kospi",
   "group": "Korea",
   "headline": "Samsung's record quarter fails to lift Seoul; KOSPI ends the day lower",
   "when": "Thu 29 Oct · Seoul session",
   "what": "Samsung Electronics reported third-quarter operating profit of ₩107.44 trillion, up 783% on a year earlier, on revenue of ₩195.25 trillion. It said 2027 high-bandwidth memory supply is already sold out. The result came in slightly short of analyst hopes. The KOSPI had touched 6,100 early on, was down 3.0% at 11:20 local time, and closed down 1.24% at 5,937.66. Samsung shares were down 6.6% mid-morning and about 4% lower by the New York close, as reported.",
   "why": "Korea is 17.4% of your portfolio. This morning your dashboard prices SCBKEQTG at its 27 Oct NAV. By Wednesday's close the KOSPI was 6.6% above that date, before Thursday's fall, so part of the net gain is not in your numbers yet. The dashboard refreshes again at 11:30, when newer NAVs usually arrive.",
   "dir": "watch",
